==English==
{{was wotd|2019|June|9}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|ἐννεάς}}, {{m|grc|ἐννεάδος||body of nine}} {{suffix|en||ad|pos2=''suffix designating a unit''}}; analysable as {{confix|en|ennea|ad}}. The Greek words {{lang|grc|ἐννεάς}} and {{lang|grc|ἐννεάδος}} are derived from {{m|grc|ἐννέᾰ||nine}}<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=62478|date=1891|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Oxford Dictionaries Online}}</ref> (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₁néwn̥||nine}}) + {{m|grc|-ᾰ́ς|pos=''suffix forming abstract nouns of number from numerals''}} or {{m|grc|-ος}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɛnɪad/}}
